ransversal.\n\n**Alternate interior angles** are the pairs of angles on *alternate* (opposite) sides of the transversal and are *interior* to (inside of) the parallel lines. These pairs of angles always have equal measure.\n\n![](images/b0/b06ff1e3d55ee09f95a1234ab4aa340d825f05971957ae8a88ff408c256c82a4.png)\n\n**Alternate external angles** are the pairs of angles on *alternate* (opposite) sides of the transversal and are *exterior* to (outside of) the parallel lines. These pairs of angles always have equal measure.\n\n![](images/4d/4d4765d2f5e49794336d2bf35705da9fa7885ce0a619dcd3a117d28cfe66645e.png)" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186193857 #edb/ref 1065 6723 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186193857 #edb/ref 1066 #uuid "17eba692-165e-58c9-96a3-8aed2c660530" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186193857 #edb/ref 1067 "Introduction" #edb/ref 17592186045417]}
